# Owner checklist

Things only you (the owner) can do. Create every account **in the company's name with a company email** you control, turn on two-factor, and keep the recovery codes safe. Invite developers as members later; never let a developer own an account.

## Now (unblocks B0 going live and B1)

- [ ] **Company email**: set up Google Workspace or Zoho on `edenacres.ng` (e.g. `admin@`, `hello@`, `security@`).
- [ ] **GitHub**: let Claude push to this repo. Either install the Claude GitHub App for `ellenhenry210/eden-acres-vision` (github.com/apps/claude), or reconnect GitHub in claude.ai → Settings → Connectors.
- [ ] **Supabase** (supabase.com): create an organisation "Eden Acres Ranch Limited" and two projects, `eden-acres-dev` and `eden-acres-prod`, region **eu-west-2 (London)** (closest to Lagos with full features). Then give the builder the URL, anon key and service-role key for dev only.
- [ ] **Vercel** (vercel.com): sign up with GitHub and import this repository. Set the production branch to `main`.
- [ ] **Domain**: in Vercel → Project → Domains, add `edenacres.ng` and `www.edenacres.ng`, then copy the DNS records Vercel shows into your registrar.
- [ ] **Paystack**: start business verification (CAC certificate, memorandum and articles, directors' IDs and BVN, utility bill, bank account in the company name).
- [ ] **Flutterwave**: start the same verification.
- [ ] **Resend** (resend.com): add the domain `edenacres.ng` and add its DNS records (SPF, DKIM) so emails don't land in spam.

